As a Premier League team, Manchester City entered the 2012–13 FA Cup in the third round, in which they were drawn at home against [[EFL Championship]] team [[Watford F.C.|Watford]]. Midway through the first half, Tevez gave Manchester City the lead with a [[Free kick (association football)|free kick]] from around {{convert|25|yd}}. [[Costel Pantilimon]] then saved a [[Fernando Forestieri]] shot for Watford. One minute before half-time, [[Gareth Barry]] doubled Manchester City's lead with a [[Header (association football)|header]]. In second-half [[stoppage time]], [[Manchester City F.C. EDS and Academy|Manchester City academy]] player [[Rony Lopes]] scored from close range to secure a 3–0 victory for his side.<ref>{{cite web |title=Man City 3–0 Watford |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/20863548 |publisher=[[BBC Sport]] |date=5 January 2013 |access-date=17 April 2013 |archive-date=8 January 2013 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130108022455/http://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/0/football/20863548 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web| url = https://www.tntsports.co.uk/football/fa-cup/2012-2013/live-manchester-city-watford_mtc570287/live.shtml| title = Manchester City 3–0 Watford| publisher = [[TNT Sports]]| access-date = 23 June 2021| date = 5 January 2013| archive-date = 25 June 2021| archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20210625101153/https://www.eurosport.com/football/fa-cup/2012-2013/live-manchester-city-watford_mtc570287/live.shtml| url-status = live}}</ref> In doing so, he became the club's youngest ever goalscorer at the age of seventeen years and eight days.<ref>{{cite web | url = https://www.espn.co.uk/football/blog/name/93/post/1846914/headline | publisher = [[ESPN]] | access-date = 23 June 2021 | title = A young star with a bright future – Marcos Lopes | first = Simon | last = Curtis | date = 9 October 2013 | archive-date = 25 June 2021 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20210625101254/https://www.espn.co.uk/football/blog/name/93/post/1846914/headline | url-status = live }}</ref> Manchester City progressed to a fourth round match against fellow Premier League side [[Stoke City F.C.|Stoke City]] away at the [[Britannia Stadium]]. Despite long spells of possession for the visiting team, the first half ended goalless. [[David Silva]] struck the Stoke goalpost and Tevez saw shots saved by the Stoke goalkeeper [[Thomas Sørensen]], before [[Pablo Zabaleta]] converted a cross from Agüero with four minutes remaining. Manchester City won the match 1–0 and progressed to the fifth round where they faced Championship side [[Leeds United F.C.|Leeds United]] at the City of Manchester Stadium.<ref>{{cite web |first=Alistair |last=Magowan |title=Stoke 0–1 Man City |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/21095877 |publisher=[[BBC Sport]] |date=5 January 2013 |access-date=17 April 2013 |archive-date=18 February 2013 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130218220655/http://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/0/football/21095877 |url-status=live }}</ref>

[[Yaya Touré]] gave Manchester City the lead in the fifth minute, taking the ball past Leeds United goalkeeper [[Jamie Ashdown]] and scoring after a pass from Tevez. Agüero then doubled his side's lead when he scored from the [[Penalty kick (association football)|penalty spot]] after he had been fouled by [[Tom Lees]]. Tevez scored Manchester City's third from close range soon after half-time before Agüero scored 15 minutes from the end of the match to secure a 4–0 victory.<ref>{{cite web |first=Phil |last=McNulty |title=Man City 4–0 Leeds United |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/21449162 |publisher=[[BBC Sport]] |authorlink=Phil McNulty |date=17 February 2013 |access-date=17 April 2013 |archive-date=14 April 2013 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130414204659/http://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/0/football/21449162 |url-status=live }}</ref> In the quarter-final, Manchester City's opponents were Championship club [[Barnsley F.C.|Barnsley]] at home.  Tevez scored the first goal for Manchester City in the eleventh minute after Silva's [[Volley (association football)|volley]] rebounded off the goalpost. [[Aleksandar Kolarov]] and Tevez then scored in quick succession to make it 3–0 at half-time. Five minutes after the interval, Tevez completed his [[hat-trick#Association football|hat-trick]], scoring from [[Samir Nasri]]'s pass. Midway through the second half, Silva scored after his initial shot was kept out by Barnsley goalkeeper [[Luke Steele (footballer)|Luke Steele]] to make it 5–0, which was the final score.<ref>{{cite web |first=Chris |last=Bevan |title=Man City 5–0 Barnsley |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/21639274 |publisher=[[BBC Sport]] |date=9 March 2013 |access-date=17 April 2013 |archive-date=14 April 2013 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130414204509/http://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/0/football/21639274 |url-status=live }}</ref>

In the semi-final, Manchester City faced defending FA Cup champions [[Chelsea F.C.|Chelsea]] for the first time in the competition since 1971, the match being held at Wembley, a [[neutral venue]].<ref>{{cite web |first=Rob |last=Bagchi |title=Chelsea and Manchester City bring rarity value to FA Cup semi-final |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/blog/2013/apr/12/chelsea-manchester-city-fa-cup-semi-final |work=[[The Guardian]] |date=12 April 2013 |access-date=17 April 2013 |archive-date=19 April 2014 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140419062749/http://www.theguardian.com/football/blog/2013/apr/12/chelsea-manchester-city-fa-cup-semi-final |url-status=live }}</ref> Ten minutes before half-time, Manchester City took the lead. Agüero's shot bounced off Chelsea's defender [[César Azpilicueta]] and the ball fell to Nasri who scored. [[Vincent Kompany]] then shot off-target shortly before half-time, and two minutes after the interval Barry's cross found Agüero, who headed the ball into the Chelsea goal off the post while goalkeeper [[Petr Čech]] remained motionless. [[Demba Ba]] then scored past Pantilimon to reduce the deficit for Chelsea but the match ended 2–1 and Manchester City progressed to the final.<ref>{{cite web |first=Phil |last=McNulty |authorlink=Phil McNulty |title=Chelsea 1–2 Man City |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/22056551 |publisher=[[BBC Sport]] |date=14 April 2013 |access-date=17 April 2013 |archive-date=17 April 2013 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130417065542/http://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/0/football/22056551 |url-status=live }}</ref>

